Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraPerpendicularBisector", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"52dc9445-878e-4d72-9b2b-0dc2395748bb"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraPerpendicularBisector"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraPerpendicularBisector", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e5795cbc-8ba3-4441-8649-9f7ab57342fc"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the point family at equal finite distance from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"8492efe2-7ffd-4e3e-8abc-f9db423046a1"],

Cell["\<\
The graph must be finite, simple, undirected and unweighted, with valid \
vertex anchors. Unsupported arguments and properties stay unevaluated. The \
head is inert until a graph-aware reader or named sampler evaluates it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"bff40454-b9ac-4215-8da2-40caf89e6084"],

Cell["\<\
One representative is one raw vertex label, including a List-valued label. \
The complete family has distinct vertices in graph vertex order and unit \
vertex density. Supported measurements are \"VertexDensity\", \
\"Cardinality\", \"CountingMeasure\", \"Subgraph\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\". \
The last measure uses the existing interior-support law. \"Graph\", \
\"EdgeDensity\", \"Length\", \"Area\" and \"Volume\" are unsupported for \
these point families.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f86ceaf9-7327-4707-933e-c25055feedf0"],

Cell["\<\
Equal anchors give their connected component; disconnected anchors give an \
empty family. This is an equidistant locus. It need not separate the anchors \
or be a line, and it does not assert an angle. InfraPlane retains its \
separating-family meaning.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"5eeb849b-9214-430c-b02c-106468305998"]
}, Open  ]],

